# Service- and application-integration-model selection rubric — PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED [SPEC:CXC-INTEGRATION-MODELS]

> Seven shapes exist for integrating a service or application with ComposeIO/ComposeBus. A platform
> CAPABILITY is sited by a fixed decision order that defaults to the ComposeServer plugin and escapes
> to a bus-native peer, a bridge, a standalone process, or (almost never) the kernel only when a
> specific, named condition holds — unchanged since 2026-09-12. An end-user APPLICATION is NOT sited
> by that rubric: its home sits on a USE-CASE x COMPLEXITY spectrum — declarative state_manager config
> <-> standalone app <-> plugin — and the end-user CHOOSES along it for their own skill, their use of
> agentic AI, and the project's complexity, deliberately without a numeric threshold deciding for them
> (David, 2026-09-12). This document is the lts-fetchable source of truth for that rubric; a
> user-facing markdown doc points at it rather than restating it.

---

